# Same as GNU Stow's built-in default ignore list, plus .DS_Store, plus an
# allowlist rule for .claude/ (see the bottom of this file).
# A package-local ignore file REPLACES the built-in list entirely (it does
# not merge with it), so the defaults are repeated here on purpose.
# See CLAUDE.md and https://www.gnu.org/software/stow/manual/stow.html

RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules

.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

\.DS_Store

# Allowlist for .claude/: ignore everything in it except settings.json.
# Stow's ignore patterns are Perl regexes, so a negative lookahead works.
# This is deliberately an allowlist rather than a list of the runtime
# directories (sessions/, cache/, telemetry/, projects/, ...): a denylist
# goes stale the moment Claude Code writes somewhere new, an allowlist
# can't. Mirrors the same approach in this package's .gitignore.
#
# The default patterns above are still required — this rule only covers
# paths under .claude/, so a stray .DS_Store at the package root would
# otherwise be symlinked straight into $HOME.
^/\.claude/(?!settings\.json$).*
